title The row that lost its number while it sat -- landing a parked lap, and the two peers' numbers the card still carries
prompt The baton, unattended: take the next agent-doable lap in mantra/ and tally/, reds first, rota row N mod 5.
think LAP N = 4095, so the rota row is 0 -- AETHER, Jupiter, why the work exists, whose sense is SOUND. The threshold page asks the lap to listen rather than scan: the claim a page keeps repeating, the question it keeps answering, and the silence where a claim used to be. I read the aether threshold, follow-our-compass at the cardinal seat, the Lindy effect at the fixed, and the-grain-and-the-crossing at the dual. Three documents, one note between them -- the compass says witness before narrative, Lindy says a checked claim stays audible while an asserted one fades, and the grain's fusion strand says a guard that cannot red guards nothing. All three are the same ear rule at three ages.
think THE ROUND OPEN HAD FILLED THE DEAD-LETTER BOX, AND THIS TIME SOMEBODY READ IT. git stash list held four records; stash@{0}, parked at 19:07:15 eighteen minutes before this lap opened, carried a COMPLETE GREEN FEATURE -- the tally roster meter's second reading, its runner calling all eleven proofs, the roster comment, a REDS shelf, a folded-accounts archive, and a session log. Nine files, 286 insertions, on no reader ref at all. That is exactly the shape %507 was booked for one lap earlier, and this is the first lap to act on that guard's finding rather than report it.
think THE NUMBER HAD BEEN SPENT WHILE THE WORK SAT. The parked row booked %509 at 20260906.180651. git fetch xy then reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next reads 510, because the fleet lane published %509 at 20260906.190934 for a different fault and that commit is HEAD. The derived-spine law decides this without a judgment call: the stamp is the key and does not move, the number is a view allocated by the anointed remote, and an UNSHARED row is the one that yields. So the row keeps 20260906.180651 and takes %510, and the shelf says so in its own second paragraph rather than leaving a reader to wonder.
think I PROVED THE PARKED WORK STILL STANDS BEFORE LANDING IT, RATHER THAN TRUSTING ITS ELDER GREEN. Two commits landed after the stash was made -- daf0d97ca moved thirty-four files into their letter rooms and 5826c9be2 repaired the seat-prompt read. Neither touched the two tool files, proven by an empty git diff between the stash base and HEAD over exactly those paths. Then I ran all six newly called witnesses on this tree: region, gardens, copy, maybe, no_padding, parse_int, every one GREEN, with git status --porcelain hashed before and after to prove the tree had not moved while the cold roster was running beside them.
think THE ELDER READING, MEASURED LIVE THIS LAP RATHER THAN QUOTED FROM THE PARKED LOG. tally_roster_scan.sh on the tree as it stood: covered=11 uncovered=0 verdict=ok. Eleven modules reported covered, and six of those eleven proofs were carried by no clock -- tally/region.rye, the one memory-carving body in the tree, named by no runner anywhere since the lap that wrote it on 20260827.
obs THE SILENCE THE AETHER ROW TRAINS YOU TO NOTICE WAS A STASH. A green witness is sound; a claim retired because it could no longer be checked is an honest silence. This lap found a third thing the threshold page does not name: a GREEN feature making no sound at all, because nothing was pointed at it. %507's guard now reports unlanded=1 parked=1, and a report only becomes a repair when a lap opens the box.
obs THE STALE NUMBERS ARE ONE DEFECT IN TWO ROOMS, AND I READ BOTH RATHER THAN ONE. session-logs/date/README-index-20260906.md carried %506 for the log at 20260906.153431 and %507 for the log at 20260906.153324. Both logs name their own row in their own text -- %504 four times and %505 once -- and the ledger's stamps agree exactly: %505 (20260906.153324). So the shelf rows were stale, which is %440's recorded shape and owes no new row (%484). What is NEW is that construction/ITINERARY.md carries the same two stale numbers in the peers' own live-front blocks, and both now resolve onto MY folded shelves -- %506 is the property nobody named, %507 is a park is not a landing. A reader following either lands on the wrong finding, silently.
obs NO GUARD READS EITHER SITE, AND THAT IS THE MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN THE COMPLAINT. index_row_bound_scan.sh reads stamps, order, and row length and answers verdict=ok with both stale numbers standing -- it has no opinion about %N at all. reds_citation_witness reads two shapes that are promises: an anchor text that IS the number, and a shelf word one line back. All four sites here are BARE %N in prose, so the citation guard cannot see them either. That is %502's class -- a number and a path naming two rows -- one room over, and the repair here is by hand.
obs I REPAIRED THE PEERS' NUMBERS RATHER THAN ONLY NAMING THEM, AND THE REASON IS BOUNDED. A landed account's number is not in-flight work, the edit is two characters, and leaving a wrong pointer on the tree's most-read living pin costs every reader who follows it. I name the repair in the commit body and here so the peers see it rather than discovering it in a diff.
obs AND THE NUMBER MOVED A SECOND TIME, AT THE SEND. The rebase before the push found xy two commits ahead, and one of them published %510 -- for the guard that reads the round open's dead-letter box, the very instrument whose finding this lap acted on. So the row went %509 -> %510 -> %511 in one lap, twice beaten by a peer while it was unshared. The derived spine decided both without a judgment call. The recital conflicted where two ships had appended a fold row; upstream's rows kept their place and mine took %511 beneath them.
obs THE CARD MET ITS BOUND AND I FOLDED MY OWN. Upstream's card stood at 40,930 of 40,960 -- thirty bytes -- so my block had no room. Rather than raise the bound or trim a peer's words, I folded two FINISHED accounts of my own: a peer's one-line condensation of my %507/%506 accounts, into the archive shelf that already holds them word for word, and my %479 paragraph into its own shelf, leaving the card's pointer. The card closes at 40,958 with the pin guard GREEN. The two stale card numbers I had repaired are moot: Petrichor and Pheromone corrected their own upstream during the same window, which is the fleet working rather than a race lost.
obs AND %440 FIRED ON MY OWN REBASE, WHICH IS THE MEASUREMENT MY PARKED LAP ASKED FOR. The rebase's three-way merge of session-logs/date/README-index-20260906.md produced 2 duplicate stamps and one misordering across 104 rows; the re-verify pass caught it and I deduped and re-sorted by hand, 104 -> 102. That is the second lap running to book the same tax, and the parked log above records the first: the hand repair is not idempotent under merge. A merge driver keyed to the shelf files is the structural answer, it lives in .git/config, and it wants %427's arming clause -- fleet infrastructure rather than my lane, named here rather than taken.
obs THE STASH NEEDS NO SURGERY, AND I READ THE GUARD RATHER THAN GUESSING. stash_record_scan.sh judges a record by asking whether any reader ref carries a file AT THE SESSION LOG'S OWN PATH -- git cat-file -e "$r:$p" over every branch and remote-tracking ref outside the pier/ namespace. So committing the parked log at its own path clears the box; dropping the stash would be destroying a record to satisfy a meter. Before this lap: stashes=4 records=4 landed=3 unlanded=1 verdict=records_unlanded.
loom guard=tally_roster wall_s=14 calls=11 added_witnesses=6 added_s=6
loom scan=tally_roster covered=11 heard=11 unheard=0 pen_legs=15
loom witnesses_reproven=6 all_green=yes tree_moved=no
loom roster=cold guards=152 wall_s=1221 green=146 red=3 gated=3 tree_moved=no
loom roster=hot guards=152 wall_s=1051 green=149 red=0 gated=3 tree_moved=no verdict=ok
obs ONE HONEST CAVEAT ON THAT GREEN. The two loom lines above were written AFTER the pass closed, so the hot green measured this tree minus those two lines. Rather than assume they could not matter -- the judgment that had already misled me twice this lap -- I re-ran the four rostered guards that read session logs: log_has_a_row, index_row_bound, ascii_document and qa_report_card, all GREEN. A third full pass for two ASCII key=value lines was not proportionate; naming which guards were re-proven, and why those four, is what makes that a measurement rather than a shrug.
obs AND THE SAME LESSON BIT ME A SECOND TIME, IN THE OTHER DIRECTION. The first hot pass read guards_run=152 guards_green=149 guards_red=0 guards_gated=3 guards_seconds=1050 -- and closed run_verdict=tree_moved, because I edited THIS FILE'S erratum while it ran. The runner digests staged, unstaged and untracked content at open and again at close, so a correction to a staged log is a tree move exactly like a code edit. HOLD STILL WHILE IT RUNS has now cost me one transient red and one refused pass in a single lap, from the two halves of the sentence I had only half read: do not compete for the machine, and do not touch the tree -- including the log you are writing. The pass was re-run over a still tree, and the number that counts is the second one.
obs THE AETHER LAP'S SECOND GIFT WAS A GUARD'S OWN HEAD SENTENCE, AND IT IS PETRICHOR'S. reds_citation_scan.sh's FOLD reader matches Rows?[ ]+[0-9]+[ ]+folded to -- a BARE number -- and its head says so plainly: "The number is bare here (Row 172, no sigil)." I reproduced its fold_links=47 exactly by hand: 34 in construction/archive/REDS-fold-index-rows-1-172.md, which is CLOSED, and 13 elder lines in the living recital. The living recital writes Row %N folded to, and 79 of its lines wear that sigil against 13 that do not -- so the reader sees the closed room and thirteen fossils, and cannot see the shape every new fold is written in, including the row this lap appends. The gap grows by one per fold. It is honest rather than false-green, since those lines sit inside their own declared unread_links=215 of 281, and the fix is one character: %?[0-9]+. Named rather than taken -- the file is one lap old and its ship is actively working the 208.
loom citation=fold_reader fold_links=47 index_closed=34 recital_bare=13 recital_sigilled_unread=79
file tools/fixtures/t/tally_roster_scan.sh -- the second reading landed from the stash: heard beside covered, unheard named, gated at zero, a call being a quoted token inside run [.
file tools/t/tally_roster_witness.rish -- all eleven per-module proofs called, seven new pen legs proving the reading from both sides; every one of the six re-run GREEN on this tree before landing.
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri -- the tally_roster row's reason: this is the room's one clock, and what it does not call is not run.
file construction/archive/REDS-a-name-is-not-a-clock-rows-510.md -- the row, renumbered from %509 with the reason written into its second paragraph.
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md -- the fold trail, naming the renumber.
file construction/archive/20260906-180832_itinerary-landed-accounts.md -- the two elder Patchouli accounts, word for word, folded to make room.
file construction/ITINERARY.md -- my block rewritten; the peers' two stale numbers repaired; the FOLD-reader gap handed to Petrichor with its measurement.
file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-180937_a-name-is-not-a-clock.kyri -- the parked round's own record, landed at its own path so stash_record_scan.sh reads the box as empty.
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260906.md -- two stale row numbers repaired, and both rounds' rows.
obs MY OWN ERRATUM, AND IT COST A FALSE RED. The cold pass closed guards_run=152 guards_green=146 guards_red=3 guards_seconds=1221 tree_moved=no. Two reds are this lap's own subject -- stash_record at unlanded=1, and standing_equipment quoting it. The third, comlink_topology, failed its control at phase depth_reads_the_outfit; run alone afterward the control reads faults=0 verdict=proven and the witness reads GREEN. The hot pass then read comlink_topology green 16s -- the same 16s it took to red -- so the failure is transient rather than a tree fault. I had run six Rye witnesses concurrently with the cold pass to pre-check the parked work, and a peer ship was compiling Glow on this pier through both passes, so load is the LEADING read rather than a proven cause: I cannot separate my contribution from the peer's. What I can state is what I did. HOLD STILL WHILE IT RUNS means the machine as well as the tree -- I read it as do not edit -- and a guard that reds under contention sends a peer chasing a phantom in their own lane. No row booked: nothing in the tree is wrong, and the honest artifact is the pair of readings rather than a diagnosis.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two doors, both one word. Standing, unchanged: the identity gap wants a fourth field on Line, since pos counts inside one weave and two branches inserting collide at one small integer, which merge refuses as PositionTextDisagrees. That word opens the merge story and the diff anchor together. New, and measured rather than argued: reds_citation's FOLD reader wants a bare number and the living recital writes the sigil, so 79 fold citations -- every one written since the sigil, including this lap's -- sit unread while the closed index's 34 are read. It is Petrichor's file and one lap old, so I named it rather than took it.
